        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-15T19:17:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think this is valuable to have this inner if and else. This is all for adding the trace events right? So I would do the tracing something like:\n\n```\n{\n    TRACE_EVENT0_ALWAYS(\"skia.shaders\", \"CreateGraphicsPipeline\");\n    if (gpu-\u003evkCaps().supportsPipelineCreationCacheControl()) {\n        TRACE_EVENT0_ALWAYS(\"skia.shaders\", \"CreateGraphicsPipeline-CacheLookupOnly\");\n        CreateGraphicsPipeline(....);\n    }\n\n    if (err \u003d\u003d VK_PIPELINE_COMPILE_REQUIRED) {\n        TRACE_EVENT0_ALWAYS(\"skia.shaders\", \"CreateGraphicsPipeline-Compile\");\n        CreateGraphicsPipeline(....);\n    }\n}\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 595,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 595,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "7ccec5fae83fb2f7b94672d187113b63c2668514",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d796f8d2_c509e1a1",
        "filename": "src/gpu/ganesh/vk/GrVkPipeline.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 595,
      "author": {
        "id": 3762617
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-16T16:42:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not entirely convinced we should do this, since when `VK_EXT_pipeline_creation_cache_control` is not available, we will be reporting compiles even for cache lookups. Unless we assume that the extension is always available for our purposes?\n\nIn other words, to emit a different tracing structure depending on whether the extension is available, we would always need the check. I think we can only avoid that if we always have the same tracing structure, however that could be a problem if we\u0027re dealing with populations where some devices have the extension enabled and others do not.\n\nHow do you think we should proceed?",
      "parentUuid": "f3f6d875_70e3d447",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 595,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 595,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "7ccec5fae83fb2f7b94672d187113b63c2668514",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fa3ce6e0_2aef5cb4",
        "filename": "src/gpu/ganesh/vk/GrVkPipeline.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 595,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-21T17:41:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So the main trace we want to track is the \"CreateGraphicsPipeline\". This tells us how much time we are spending in the driver to eventually have a VkPipeline. This trace is also stable whether or not we have the extension. So this is the value we\u0027ll be doing most of our \"perf\" analysis on. The sub traces are purely meant to give us more insight into what\u0027s happening on the hood.\n\nBasically there are two cases we\u0027ll call into vkCreateGrahicsPipeline. Once with the VK_PIPELINE_CREATE_FAIL_ON_PIPELINE_COMPILE_REQUIRED_BIT_EXT flag set and one without. So IMO I think its fine to just have one trace for each of these options and keeps the code simpler. It\u0027s not like it will be hard to figure out if the extension is on the device or not since if it is we\u0027ll always have a \"CreateGraphicsPipeline-CacheLookupOnly\" call. If you have a better suggestion for \"CreateGraphicsPipeline-Compile\" since as you said it doesn\u0027t always compile (when we don\u0027t have the extension).\n\nThat being said I\u0027m also fine if y\u0027all really thing a different trace structure is better. Between you and Noelle you have more experience looking at the traces for compiles.",
      "parentUuid": "d796f8d2_c509e1a1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 595,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 595,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "7ccec5fae83fb2f7b94672d187113b63c2668514",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "06b938ca_7e183d47",
        "filename": "src/gpu/ganesh/vk/GrVkPipeline.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 595,
      "author": {
        "id": 3762617
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-22T13:41:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Okay, I\u0027m happy if we\u0027re going to only be looking at `CreateGraphicsPipeline` most of the time anyway. We could use `CreateGraphicsPipeline-PotentialCompile`, but that will be more confusing when the extension is enabled, and presumably more and more devices are going to have that extension over time. So I\u0027m happy to apply the changes as originally suggested.\n\nIf Noelle has additional suggestions I\u0027m happy to apply them.",
      "parentUuid": "fa3ce6e0_2aef5cb4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 595,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 595,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "7ccec5fae83fb2f7b94672d187113b63c2668514",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "057e9196_445b25aa",
        "filename": "src/gpu/ganesh/vk/GrVkPipeline.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 595,
      "author": {
        "id": 19099
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-22T15:37:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m OK with either approach, and am hesitant to extend review further.\n\nTrying to think through interpretations -- with the current approach, if average values of `CreateGraphicsPipeline-Compile` are compared between devices that do and do not support the extension (or if the extension is supported with a driver upgrade), then the metric will appear to regress on devices that _do_ support the extension, since it will no longer be \"diluted\" by unreported cache hits? I could see it being initially confusing, but perhaps not an issue in practice.\n\nI personally use Code Search for understanding trace slices -- perhaps we just add a short comment noting the potential misnomer?",
      "parentUuid": "06b938ca_7e183d47",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 595,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 595,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "7ccec5fae83fb2f7b94672d187113b63c2668514",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b6cdd131_78538266",
        "filename": "src/gpu/ganesh/vk/GrVkPipeline.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 595,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-22T16:58:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Okay talking this over a little more with Noelle offline, I think we should go back to something closer to what you had before. Even though we know what the subtraces might mean in certain cases, someone else trying to look at different traces may not understand that the meaning and possible range of values may change depending on the extension being present or not.\n\nSo that leaves us still with the one high level `CreateGraphicsPipeline`, but then have 3 possible sub traces. Those would be (feel free to come up with better names):\n`CreateGraphicsPipeline-CacheLookupOnly` // We have extension and setting fail on compile flag\n`CreateGraphicsPipeline-CompileAfterCacheMiss` // Have extension but failed first call\n`CreateGraphicsPipeline-Compile` // Don\u0027t have the extension.\n\nThanks for bearing with us as we bikesheded on this. If you want you can make the inner if block (which picks between the extension vs not extension compile), just control a static string to pick, and then pass that into a TRACE call. That avoids duplicated the calls to `vkCreateGraphicsPipelines`. But it is not a big deal either way.",
      "parentUuid": "057e9196_445b25aa",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 595,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 595,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "7ccec5fae83fb2f7b94672d187113b63c2668514",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0e71005a_075814af",
        "filename": "src/gpu/ganesh/vk/GrVkPipeline.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 595,
      "author": {
        "id": 3762617
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-23T14:21:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks both, I\u0027ve done that.\n\nI went with these labels:\n - `CacheLookup`: dropped the `Only` suffix as this seems redundant with the new, clear structure\n - `CompileAfterCacheMiss`: left as-is, describes exactly what happened\n - `CacheLookupOrCompile`: since we don\u0027t know which one happened exactly and the times will fluctuate to reflect this (so `Compile` by itself could be misleading)\n \nHappy to do another round if anyone has better name suggestions.\n\nI could not choose a static string at runtime - I ran into this compile error:\n```\nexternal/perfetto/include/perfetto/tracing/internal/track_event_data_source.h:142:7: error: static assertion failed due to requirement \u0027IsValidEventNameType\u003cconst char *, void\u003e::value\u0027: Event names must be static strings. To use dynamic event names, see https://perfetto.dev/docs/in\nstrumentation/track-events#dynamic-event-names         \n```\nso I\u0027ve resorted to the if / else block.\n\nI had this code:\n```\nTRACE_EVENT0_ALWAYS(\n    \"skia.shaders\",\n         gpu-\u003evkCaps().supportsPipelineCreationCacheControl() ? \n             \"CreateGraphicsPipeline-CompileAfterCacheMiss\" : \n             \"CreateGraphicsPipeline-CacheLookupOrCompile\");\n```\n\nIf there\u0027s a better way to do this please let me know!",
      "parentUuid": "b6cdd131_78538266",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 595,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 595,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "7ccec5fae83fb2f7b94672d187113b63c2668514",
